(4198732, 602868, 77196, '<td valign="top">This looks like Dr. Achoo - if not, take that as a huge compliment. I can''t decide if I like the rainbow umbrella against the strong yellow colors in the photo. It is a very strong contrast / contradiction. Regardless of "like" or "don''t like" this is a very striking photo.</td>', 'This looks like Dr. Achoo - if not, take that as a huge compliment. I can''t decide if I like the rainbow umbrella against the strong yellow colors in the photo. It is a very strong contrast / contradiction. Regardless of "like" or "don''t like" this is a very striking photo.', '2007-10-27 00:40:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(4198827, 602006, 75034, '<td valign="top">A beautiful and fresh approach to this challenge. you have a fine shot. I like the lighting and the colour, not to overdone and the reflections are beautiful. I''m pleased to see that you have placed your subject off center and allowed the ripples in the water to carry the shot. This has a warm feel to it and the tones are just right. Wonderful capture. I hope it does well here.</td>', 'A beautiful and fresh approach to this challenge. you have a fine shot. I like the lighting and the colour, not to overdone and the reflections are beautiful. I''m pleased to see that you have placed your subject off center and allowed the ripples in the water to carry the shot. This has a warm feel to it and the tones are just right. Wonderful capture. I hope it does well here.', '2007-10-27 01:18:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(4198838, 602652, 75034, '<td valign="top">I like the concept, but the soft focus on the eye makes me look for other parts of the image that are in focus. I would offer one thing and that would be that you be tack sharp on the eye and move everything else ouy of focus. I think that would have helped your chances here. That being said maybe you wanted the soft focus and in that case I would have wanted to see that reflected in the title so we wouldn''t have to draw our own conclusions.<br/> <br/>Soft Rainbow Vision or A Vision of Soft Rainbows, I''m sure you see what I mean.</td>', 'I like the concept, but the soft focus on the eye makes me look for other parts of the image that are in focus. I would offer one thing and that would be that you be tack sharp on the eye and move everything else ouy of focus. I think that would have helped your chances here. That being said maybe you wanted the soft focus and in that case I would have wanted to see that reflected in the title so we wouldn''t have to draw our own conclusions. Soft Rainbow Vision or A Vision of Soft Rainbows, I''m sure you see what I mean.', '2007-10-27 01:26:26.000000', NULL, 1),
