(4202894, 603083, 7810, '<td valign="top">Way to go Rudy !!!<br/>Huge Congrats<br/>Glad to see you on the front page with this awesome image.</td>', 'Way to go Rudy !!!Huge CongratsGlad to see you on the front page with this awesome image.', '2007-10-29 05:29:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4202897, 601015, 57229, '<td valign="top">I see you one place below me - no fair, but nice company and we got in the top 100 :)<br/> <br/>This is a very fresh idea. I think maybe (if you were the sort of votes hawk that spends massive amounts of time and energy setting up shots) that it could me more effective against either a blurred out (bokeh) window/garden background or just a landscape picture of some sort, as well as the whole thing being stood up vertical - tea bags fixed somehow - with the rainbow more like a twelve o'' clock to three o'' clock quadrant and the honey pot inside it but less central. Maybe any old background would do, but preferably less intrusive/less in focus. I''m just thinking the effect could be a little lighter and airier (?) with a sort of off centre orientation.<br/> <br/>Don''t mind me, just thinking out loud.</td>', 'I see you one place below me - no fair, but nice company and we got in the top 100 :) This is a very fresh idea. I think maybe (if you were the sort of votes hawk that spends massive amounts of time and energy setting up shots) that it could me more effective against either a blurred out (bokeh) window/garden background or just a landscape picture of some sort, as well as the whole thing being stood up vertical - tea bags fixed somehow - with the rainbow more like a twelve o'' clock to three o'' clock quadrant and the honey pot inside it but less central. Maybe any old background would do, but preferably less intrusive/less in focus. I''m just thinking the effect could be a little lighter and airier (?) with a sort of off centre orientation. Don''t mind me, just thinking out loud.', '2007-10-29 05:31:55.000000', NULL, 0),
