(4203397, 601015, 66384, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by raish:</b></div><hr/><i> I see you one place below me - no fair, but nice company and we got in the top 100 :)<br/> <br/>This is a very fresh idea. I think maybe (if you were the sort of votes hawk that spends massive amounts of time and energy setting up shots) that it could me more effective against either a blurred out (bokeh) window/garden background or just a landscape picture of some sort, as well as the whole thing being stood up vertical - tea bags fixed somehow - with the rainbow more like a twelve o'' clock to three o'' clock quadrant and the honey pot inside it but less central. Maybe any old background would do, but preferably less intrusive/less in focus. I''m just thinking the effect could be a little lighter and airier (?) with a sort of off centre orientation.<br/> <br/>Don''t mind me, just thinking out loud. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Raish, thank you for an excellent idea. Where were you when I needed you. I shot this photo in a room using available light from a picture window overlooking a Lake Superior beach. It was taken on a desk with a scotch tape dispenser on it. Why didn''t I think of taping the tea bags to the window? *bangs head on wall*</td>', 'Originally posted by raish: I see you one place below me - no fair, but nice company and we got in the top 100 :) This is a very fresh idea. I think maybe (if you were the sort of votes hawk that spends massive amounts of time and energy setting up shots) that it could me more effective against either a blurred out (bokeh) window/garden background or just a landscape picture of some sort, as well as the whole thing being stood up vertical - tea bags fixed somehow - with the rainbow more like a twelve o'' clock to three o'' clock quadrant and the honey pot inside it but less central. Maybe any old background would do, but preferably less intrusive/less in focus. I''m just thinking the effect could be a little lighter and airier (?) with a sort of off centre orientation. Don''t mind me, just thinking out loud.  Raish, thank you for an excellent idea. Where were you when I needed you. I shot this photo in a room using available light from a picture window overlooking a Lake Superior beach. It was taken on a desk with a scotch tape dispenser on it. Why didn''t I think of taping the tea bags to the window? *bangs head on wall*', '2007-10-29 11:10:49.000000', NULL, 0),
