(4210114, 603137, 67579, '<td valign="top">Awesome thanks <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=53316" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">klstover</a> I forgot completely that I hit that little magic button, I usually avoid it LOL.<br/> <br/>Thanks so much for the comments though I really appreciated your time and thoughts :)<br/> <br/>-dave</td>', 'Awesome thanks  klstover I forgot completely that I hit that little magic button, I usually avoid it LOL. Thanks so much for the comments though I really appreciated your time and thoughts :) -dave', '2007-10-31 23:09:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4210196, 600656, 67697, '<td valign="top">This is so cool.  Your eyes are amazing!  I love your take on this challenge and I am glad the voters for the most part, gave you a decent score.</td>', 'This is so cool.  Your eyes are amazing!  I love your take on this challenge and I am glad the voters for the most part, gave you a decent score.', '2007-10-31 23:42:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4211035, 603233, 53316, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Comment:<br/> <br/>Well as people have said, the background was something that really hurt you.  I do think that the sheet, even wrinkled, was better than having a ton of even more distracting elements in the background.<br/> <br/>The rainbow, wow, you did a great job with that. I never would have guessed that it was from a CD.<br/> <br/>The pot at the bottom blends into the background a lot, so maybe having a bit of a more well-lit area down there would have helped.<br/> <br/>Overall I thought that this was really creative and had a lot of potential. It made me smile when I came across it during voting because it''s something happy and cheerful (a pot of gold, yay!) and you don''t see images like this all the time.</td>', 'Critique Club Comment: Well as people have said, the background was something that really hurt you.  I do think that the sheet, even wrinkled, was better than having a ton of even more distracting elements in the background. The rainbow, wow, you did a great job with that. I never would have guessed that it was from a CD. The pot at the bottom blends into the background a lot, so maybe having a bit of a more well-lit area down there would have helped. Overall I thought that this was really creative and had a lot of potential. It made me smile when I came across it during voting because it''s something happy and cheerful (a pot of gold, yay!) and you don''t see images like this all the time.', '2007-11-01 04:25:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4213742, 602541, 84684, '<td valign="top">This is absolutely beautiful!!!!!!</td>', 'This is absolutely beautiful!!!!!!', '2007-11-01 21:13:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4213798, 602397, 21367, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critque Club.<br/> <br/>Very nice shot Gennaro.  You have captured the telling of the story well here with the gentleman''s eyes. <br/> <br/>A technically sound composition with a nice crop, great catch lights and questioning expression of the model.  The black background forces the viewer back to the face and the eyes draw us in.<br/> <br/>For me the detail of the paint on the gentleman''s face is almost too sharp as some of the sharp edges draw my eye to the left side of the shot, away from the eyes which I want to focus on.  The red line and gold spot, which need to be in the shot to finish the story, seem to overpower the eyes.<br/> <br/>Perhaps softening the shot with a gaussian blur layer and then lightly erasing the eyes back through would give the shot a dreamy inquizitive feel and take just a bit of the face paint white areas and colored.<br/> <br/>This is a great expressive shot, very creative.  It is an interesting take of a rainbow for the challenge.  Voters of DPC are sometimes unfairly set in what a challenge description means to them, and will sometimes give lessor score to shots they don''t understand.<br/> <br/>Great Job<br/>Andy<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critque Club. Very nice shot Gennaro.  You have captured the telling of the story well here with the gentleman''s eyes.  A technically sound composition with a nice crop, great catch lights and questioning expression of the model.  The black background forces the viewer back to the face and the eyes draw us in. For me the detail of the paint on the gentleman''s face is almost too sharp as some of the sharp edges draw my eye to the left side of the shot, away from the eyes which I want to focus on.  The red line and gold spot, which need to be in the shot to finish the story, seem to overpower the eyes. Perhaps softening the shot with a gaussian blur layer and then lightly erasing the eyes back through would give the shot a dreamy inquizitive feel and take just a bit of the face paint white areas and colored. This is a great expressive shot, very creative.  It is an interesting take of a rainbow for the challenge.  Voters of DPC are sometimes unfairly set in what a challenge description means to them, and will sometimes give lessor score to shots they don''t understand. Great JobAndy ', '2007-11-01 21:33:39.000000', NULL, 0),
